{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01BVmMyjeybr61UT4txmCps3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/06-013-debug-model-that-runs-but-doesnt-learn-broadcasting-dimensio.md`** covering:\n\n- **Mini-batch overfit test** as the first gate — any correctly wired model must memorise 32 examples in 100 steps; if it can't, data scale is irrelevant\n- **Broadcasting traps** — PyTorch silently reshapes mismatched tensors (e.g. `labels.T` of shape `(1,B)` against `(B,C)` logits), producing finite but meaningless loss; fix with explicit `assert` before the loss call\n- **Gradient `None`-check** — `p.grad is None` exposes detached tensors from stray `.numpy()` or `detach()` calls; `torch.autograd.set_detect_anomaly(True)` for NaN/Inf\n- **Optimiser hygiene** — `zero_grad()` placement, LR scale, `loss.mean()` vs `loss.sum()`\n- **Concrete BERT incident** — loss plateau at `ln(num_classes)` traced to accidental `.detach()` on the embedding layer\n- 3 pitfalls and cross-links to Q3 (perf debugging), Q9 (bias-variance), Q22 (gradient descent)\n\n13 of 26 questions complete. Next up: Q14 — Statistics (probability, distributions, regression, Bayesian, hypothesis testing)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":69728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":380,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f553d4c-6389-4d9f-bf0a-23691932d73d","uuid":"e59596d6-d70a-4c1a-95f1-236191dfb69d"}
